From: SM-G955N Ubuntu port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] hwc2 compatibility: match declared sideband C ABI

The public header and glibc dlsym wrapper take native_handle_t*, whereas this
implementation used const native_handle_t*. C++ treats that as a new overload
without the prior extern-C declaration: only a mangled symbol was exported.
Match the declared parameter; forwarding it to the const HAL method preserves
behavior and exports the actual wrapper's expected C name. Apache-2.0 notices
in the original file remain unchanged.

--- a/compat/hwc2/hwc2_compatibility_layer.cpp
+++ b/compat/hwc2/hwc2_compatibility_layer.cpp
@@ -377,7 +377,7 @@
     return static_cast<hwc2_error_t>(error);
 }
 hwc2_error_t hwc2_compat_layer_set_sideband_stream(hwc2_compat_layer_t* layer,
-                                            const native_handle_t* stream)
+                                            native_handle_t* stream)
 {
     hal::Error error = layer->self->setSidebandStream(stream);
     return static_cast<hwc2_error_t>(error);
